6,385 | +4.5% | 14.0% | 894 | 82 | 812 | 600 | 55 | 567 |\nSourcing: FY27 sales +5.3%, EBITDA margin 12.65%, EPS $11.80 \u2014 midpoint of company guidance [Actual \u2014 company IR]. Capex FY27 $35\u201340M [Actual \u2014 company IR, call transcript]. FY28+ growth and margin path: [Assumption \u2014 anchored to company's $7B/14% five-year intermediate target [Actual \u2014 company IR]; note: the $7B target assumes M&A, which my base case excludes. If no M&A, my base-case sales reach $6.38B by FY31; M&A of ~1.5\u20132%/yr closes the gap to $7B (see bull case).] D&A, capex, interest escalation beyond FY27: [Assumption]. Normalized \u0394WC + other OCF drag \u2248 $60M/yr [Estimate \u2014 5-yr average WC consumption \u2248 $40M plus other items].\nFY27 EPS check: NI $440M / 37.2M shares \u2248 $11.83 \u2014 within guidance $11.65\u201312.15 [Arithmetic].\n\nStep 3-3 Terminal value: T = 567 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.084 \u2212 0.03) = $10,069M [Arithmetic]\nTerminal growth 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 \u2248 long-run nominal GDP minus distributor maturity discount]. Implied terminal EV/EBITDA = 11.3x \u2014 roughly historical distributor normal.\nStep 3-4 DCF result [Arithmetic]:\nPV FCFs at 8.4%: 379 + 384 + 383 + 380 + 379 = $1,905M\nPV of TV: 10,069 / 1.497 = $6,726M\nEV = $8,631M | Equity = $8,631 \u2212 356 = $8,275M | Per share = $225\nSensitivity: WACC 8.0% \u2192 $259 | WACC 7.5% \u2192 $290 | Terminal 13x EBITDA \u2192 $250 | Terminal 15x EBITDA \u2192 $280\nCross-check with no-WC-normalization (company FCF definition): \u2248 $258. Central DCF: $230\u2013260.\n\nStep 3-5 Multiples cross-check:\n- FY27 EPS mid $11.90 [Actual]; quality-distributor peer GWW fwd P/E 29.6x [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo Finance]; FAST ~31x trailing [Estimate \u2014 KoalaGains]. AIT's smaller scale, less global diversification, and ~4\u20136% organic growth (vs GWW ~6\u20138%) justify a discount \u2192 22\u201325x fwd.\n- Fair value by multiple: 22x \u2192 $262 | 25x \u2192 $298.\nStep 3-6 Blended base intrinsic value: 60% DCF (~$250) + 40% multiple (~$280) = $265.\nStep 3-7 Reverse DCF (what the market is pricing):\nAt $338, with the company's own FCF path: requires either (a) WACC \u2248 7.0% with 12x terminal, or (b) WACC 8.4% with terminal exit at 18\u201320x EBITDA \u2014 i.e., a permanent re-rating comparable to a software/platform multiple. Both are aggressive; (b) is the market's implicit bet that AIT is no longer a cyclical distributor.\nStep 3-8 Tornado \u2014 top 3 variables (become Thesis KPIs):\n1. EBITDA margin trajectory to 14% (range 12.5\u201315% \u2192 IV $210\u2013$300)\n2. Terminal multiple compression (11\u201318x \u2192 IV $225\u2013$335)\n3. Sustained organic growth 4.5\u20138% (\u2192 IV $245\u2013$290)\n\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3.5-1 Competitive response: Fastenal expanding vending/on-site; Grainger at scale. If AIT's automation push succeeds, rivals replicate via partnerships (Fastenal has ~25% service revenue growth ambitions). Competitive response score: \u22121 (mild offset).\nStep 3.5-2 Reflexivity: Positive \u2014 rising stock enables cheap M&A currency and attracts automation talent (SBC $13M, modest). Negative \u2014 a de-rating would slow M&A and signal mix-shift failure. Watch V-shaped moves.\nStep 3.5-3 Customer evolution: Early adopters (semis, data centers) \u2192 mainstream (general manufacturing). As penetration rises, attach rates for technical services should lift ES gross margins; however, mainstream customers are more price-sensitive. This is the key bull/bear divergence.\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 4-1/2 Scenario table:\n| Scenario | Prob | Path | FY29 normalized EPS | Exit multiple | Price |\n|----------|------|------|--------------------|---------------|-------|\n| Bear | 25% | US industrial recession; FY27 sales \u22122%, FY28 \u22123%, margin 10.5\u201311%; ES organic <0%; LIFO/inflation persist | $9.20 | 16x | $150 |\n| Base | 50% | Guidance achieved; organic 4.5\u20135.5%; margin reaches 14% by FY31; no M&A | $14.20 | 20x (blended DCF/multiple) | $265 |\n| Bull | 25% | Automation super-cycle; ES organic >12%; M&A adds 1.5\u20132%/yr; sales \u2248 $6.9B, EBITDA margin 14.5% by FY31 | $16.50 | 22x | $360 |\nStep 4-3 Bayesian update: Prior (base 50%, bull 25%, bear 25%) informed by base rates. Update triggers already observed: FY26 Q4 organic +9.7%, ES orders double-digit 3 consecutive quarters, backlog up YoY and sequentially, July orders mid-20s growth [Actual \u2014 company IR/call]. Weight of evidence raises bull to 25% (vs mix-shift base rate 20\u201330%). Bear maintained at 25% because 10Y at 4.7% and trade-policy uncertainty are live risks; guidance itself flags H2 FY27 caution [Actual \u2014 company IR].\nStep 4-4 Expected value: EV = 0.25\u00d7150 + 0.50\u00d7265 + 0.25\u00d7360 = $260.\nStep 4-5 Margin of safety: MoS = (260 \u2212 337.93) / 260 = \u221223.1%. Negative. 50% CI $225\u2013$310; 80% CI $160\u2013$375.\n\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25