00\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n KPI (all [Actual] at source)                     Threshold \u2192 action\n 1. Quarterly organic growth vs guide (Q1: 6\u20138%)  <3% for 2 qtrs \u2192 thesis damage, halve\n 2. EBITDA margin (FY27 guide 12.5\u201312.8%)         <12.3% FY27 \u2192 downgrade target path\n 3. ES order growth (July: +mid-20s)               Flat/negative 2 qtrs \u2192 cycle alert\n 4. Automation organic growth (>20%)               <10% 3 qtrs \u2192 premium deflation risk\n 5. LIFO expense (guide $24\u201328M)                   >$35M \u2192 inflation worse, margin risk\n 6. ISM Manufacturing (Jul: 55.6)                  <48 for 3 months \u2192 activate bear case\n 7. 10Y Treasury (Aug: 4.71%)                      >5% \u2192 re-run at WACC 9%+\n 8. M&A deployment ($2B capacity)                  >$500M deal or leverage >1.5x \u2192 audit\n 9. Buyback pace (FY26: $317M)                     Pause + leverage rising \u2192 capital-allocation flag\n10. Net leverage (0.2x)                            >1.5x \u2192 thesis downgrade\n11. Share count (FY26 \u22122.5%)                       Issuance >0 \u2192 quality flag\n12. Operating NWC (14.7% of rev)                   \u0394NWC drain >15% of \u0394rev \u2192 cash-quality flag\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. SHORT THESIS (same data):\n  1. 28.4x FY27E EPS / 19x EV/EBITDA for a 12.5%-EBITDA-margin cyclical\n     distributor = software-company multiple on a truck-and-warehouse\n     business; PEG 2.9 vs Stalwart rule of ~1.\n  2. ISM at 55.6 is a cyclical high; AIT has \u22128% organic years (FY16, FY20);\n     a normal correction cuts EPS ~20% AND the multiple at once.\n  3. 14% EBITDA margin requires +150bps from 12.4% \u2014 top-decile for\n     distribution; FAST (the best) does ~22% but with vending density AIT\n     does not have; base rate of success ~30%.\n  4. Rising rates: 10Y 4.7%\u21925%+ (survey plurality) compresses every\n     long-duration multiple; AIT's own multiple is the most extended input\n     in the model.\n  5. $2B M&A capacity is a double-edged sword \u2014 distribution history is\n     littered with value-destroying rollups at cycle peaks.\n  6. 98.6% institutional ownership + a 30-point analyst band (all $390\u2013420)\n     = consensus crowded long; no marginal buyer cushion if the cycle turns.\n  7. The technology vertical (~15% of ES, ~7% of total sales) carries an\n     AI/data-center halo that can deflate as fast as it inflated.\n\nStep 9-2. LOGIC COMBAT: Long 6.5/10 vs Short 5.5/10 \u2192 gap 1.0 < 2.0 \u2192\n  conviction DOWNGRADE applied (High \u2192 borderline High, sizing already 0%).\n  The short side's weakest link: it ignores that AIT's margin step-up is\n  5 years old (not a peak artifact) and that the balance sheet (0.2x) and\n  buyback engine cap downside. The long side's weakest link: it requires\n  the market to keep paying 22x+ for a mid-margin distributor.\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: no active short-seller or activist campaign\n  identified [Unconfirmed \u2014 none found]; the only negative web claims are\n  generic (\"no economic moat,\" \"valuation disputes\") without specifics.\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments (dismissed, with resurrection conditions):\n  \u2022 \"P/E rich vs own history\" \u2192 dismissed for the bull base because sector\n    re-rated (FAST 40x) and AIT's growth/margin trajectory is improving;\n    resurrects if automation growth <10% for 3 quarters.\n  \u2022 \"Revenue growth will collapse post-reshoring cycle\" \u2192 dismissed while\n    ES orders +mid-20s and backlog rising; resurrects if ISM <48.\n  \u2022 \"LIFO is a red flag\" \u2192 dismissed (accounting policy, reverses in\n    disinflation); resurrects only as a margin-cleanliness warning.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nA. Methodology: PASS \u2014 engine blend justified (Step 0); no DCF-only, no\n   multiple-only, no TAM-only conclusions.\nB. Valuation: PASS with flags \u2014 discount rate sourced to current 10Y [Actual];\n   ERP [Assumption] and beta [Estimate] disclosed; terminal g 2.5% \u2264 nominal\n   GDP [Assumption]; single-point avoided via 50/80% CIs.\nC. Bias: PASS \u2014 pre-mortem and red team executed; consensus not followed\n   (mean target $400 is above our IV); no position-influenced anchoring.\nD. Consistency: PASS \u2014 TTM series correctly withheld by pack (fiscal anchor\n   mismatch); we did not mix T-1 (FY26) and Tpf (Aug-26 guidance) figures;\n   net-debt components explicitly chosen (LT debt + leases \u2212 cash) with the\n   overlap caveat declared.\nE. Narrative: PASS \u2014 every forward driver sourced or labelled [Assumption];\n   no \"large long-term potential\" language.\nF. Red team: PASS \u2014 short thesis 7 bullets; logic gap 1.0 disclosed and\n   applied as a conviction haircut.\nG. Data integrity: FAILED ITEMS (carried, not hidden): segment revenue/margin\n   [Unconfirmed \u2014 pack has zero dimensional rows]; total-debt composition\n   [Unconfirmed \u2014 pack cannot verify tag overlap]; FY2028+ sell-side EPS\n   [Unconfirmed \u2014 not retrieved cleanly; used own model]; DXY, credit\n   spreads, options skew, index membership, insider transactions\n   [Unconfirmed]. None of these would flip the conclusion within its CI;\n   each is reflected in the width of the 80% CI.\n\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  Date: 2026-08-24 | T0 price $337.93 | Blended IV $260 (50% CI 230\u2013320)\n  Key assumptions logged: WACC 8.4% (rf 4.7% + 0.85\u00d74.5%); FY27 +5.5% rev\n  (guided 4.0\u20136.5%); OI margin 11.2%\u219212.5% (guided EBITDA 12.5\u201312.8%, target\n  14%); terminal g 2.5%; tax 24%; \u0394NWC 10% of \u0394rev; capex 0.7% of rev.\n  Red-team concerns logged: multiple at top of own-history band; ISM cyclical\n  high; 14% EBITDA margin base rate ~30%; M&A risk on $2B; rates >5% risk.\n  Revisit triggers: quarterly organic <3%; FY27 EBITDA margin <12.3%;\n  automation <10%; ISM <48; 10Y >5%; any >$500M acquisition.\n\nSECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  ACTION:            HOLD (existing) /