vity (each \u22123 to +3):\n- Interest-rate sensitivity: \u22121 (industrial MRO spending moderately rate-sensitive)\n- Dollar sensitivity: +1 (mostly domestic; 0.4% FX benefit in Q4 [Actual \u2014 company IR])\n- Liquidity sensitivity: +1 (M&A-dependent growth, but FCF-funded)\n- Economic-cycle sensitivity: +2 (MRO/automation tied to industrial production)\n- Commodity sensitivity: +1 (LIFO expense is an inflation pass-through drag: FY26 $21.5M, FY27 guide $24\u201328M [Actual \u2014 company IR])\nWeighted expected macro impact: +0.3 (slightly positive) \u2014 Reflation is modestly favorable to industrial distributors.\nMacro alignment: Neutral-to-light Tailwind. Conviction +0.5 step. Macro does not change intrinsic value.\n\nSECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 1.5-1 Base rates:\n- 5-year survival, mature industrial distributor: >95% [Estimate \u2014 sector base rate]\n- Continued 4\u20137% organic growth from a $5B industrial distributor: ~50\u201360% [Estimate]\n- Successful secular mix-shift (distribution \u2192 technical solutions/automation): ~20\u201330% [Estimate]\n- Large M&A (>$10B) creating ROIC > WACC: 25\u201335% [Reference]; AIT deploys <$1B tuck-ins \u2014 materially higher success base rate, ~40\u201350% [Estimate]\nStep 1.5-2 Deviation from base rate:\nBase case assumes 50\u201360% probability of achieving mid-single-digit growth \u2014 consistent with base rate. The bull case assumes a durable automation re-rating \u2014 above the 20\u201330% mix-shift base rate. Justification: (1) Engineered Solutions organic +12.9%, automation >20% for 4 years [Actual \u2014 company IR]; (2) technology vertical now >15% of ES segment [Actual \u2014 company IR]; (3) 3 consecutive quarters of double-digit ES order growth [Actual \u2014 company IR]. Acceptable deviation \u2014 evidence-based.\nStep 1.5-3 Base-rate shock check: Bull success probability 25% \u2248 base rate 20\u201330%. No red flag. No success assumption exceeds 2x base rate.\n\nSECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2-1 Understanding: AIT is a value-added distributor of industrial motion, fluid power, flow-control and automation components. It sells MRO supplies and engineered technical solutions to North American plants and OEMs, and is shifting mix toward higher-margin engineered systems and automation. Understandability: High.\n\nStep 2-2 Moat assessment (0\u20133 each):\nIntangible assets (technical expertise, brands): 2 | Switching costs (embedded MRO relationships): 2 | Network effects: 1 | Cost advantage: 1 | Scale: 2 | Regulatory barriers: 1 | Data moat: 1 \u2192 Total 10/21 = Narrow moat, with signs of widening: ES segment growing 2x Service Center, backlog rising [Actual \u2014 company IR].\nStep 2-3 Lynch classification: Fast Grower (revenue +8.8% FY26, EPS +8.2% [Actual]). Checkpoints: institutionalized growth, manageable cyclicality, balance sheet strength \u2014 all pass.\n\nStep 2-4 Financial strength scorecard:\n- Revenue 3-yr CAGR (FY23\u201326): +4.0% [Arithmetic]; last-4Q YoY: +7.3% to +10.4% accelerating [Filed]\n- Operating margin: FY26 11.1% vs 12-yr median 7.0% [Arithmetic] \u2014 clear structural improvement\n- ROE: 22.4% [Aggregator]; ROIC \u2248 NOPAT $412M / IC ~$2.0B \u2248 20% [Estimate]\n- FCF margin: 9.3% (company-def FCF $461M / sales $4.967B) [Actual]\n- Net debt: $356M lease-adjusted \u2248 0.6x EBITDA [Arithmetic]; gross interest coverage >20x [Arithmetic]\n- Judgment: Excellent\n\nStep 2-5 Capital allocation scorecard (15 pts):\nBuyback efficiency: 3 (1.2M sh at ~$264 avg vs $338 current \u2014 bought below fair value) | M&A track record: 2 (Hydrodyne double-digit growth, +200bp EBITDA margin [Actual]; broader track record [Unconfirmed]) | Capex efficiency: 3 (capex only 0.5% of sales, incremental ROIC very high [Arithmetic]) | Mix rationality: 3 (buybacks + tuck-in M&A + dividend, disciplined) | Guidance accuracy: 3 (FY26 raised, Q4 beat, FY27 issued above prior [Actual]) \u2192 14/15. Insider ownership 0.76% [Aggregator] \u2014 no bonus/penalty.\n\nSECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2.5-1 R&D capitalization: Not material \u2014 distributor, no meaningful in-house R&D [Actual \u2014 expense structure]. No adjustment.\nStep 2.5-2 SBC treatment: SBC $13M FY26 [Filed]. Owner FCF = reported FCF \u2212 SBC: $461M \u2212 $13M = $448M [Arithmetic]. Per-share growth: share count \u22122.5% 1-yr, \u22120.8% 3-yr CAGR [Filed].\nStep 2.5-3 Operating lease capitalization: Add $221M leases to debt [Filed] \u2192 adjusted net debt $356M. EBIT/interest + lease interest \u2248 40x [Arithmetic] \u2014 comfortable